WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-Guys, as you know, I have a new
children's book out.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.567
"Nana Loves You More,"
and it just came out this week.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.834
It just came out this week,
and I was excited.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:12.133
We had Nana-themed week
and all sorts of talented

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.667
grandmas came, and it was
awesome and I loved it.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.767
It just got announced today
that we are number one on

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.367
"The New York Times" best-seller
list.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:21.367
Come on!

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.300
[ Applause ]

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.501
Number one, baby.
-Best-seller.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.033
-I'm just so psyched about that.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.834
Look, it's very thin.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.200
-Right.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.167
-You know, and it looks like no
work went into this.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:38.901
-Right, but...
-Well, you know,

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:40.534
I did put some work into it.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.234
-Yeah.
-Figuring out the end?

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.167
-I'm figuring out --
-Have you won it?

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.801
-No, but look at this.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:55.567
This thing,
it took two years to make.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.801
And I'm serious.
It did.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:58.801
Because you come up
with the idea,

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.267
I go, "Oh, yeah.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.834
I want to do something
for grandmas out there."

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.868
And so you write --
I had like one good line.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.167
I go, "Okay, that's good."
And it's a little weepy.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.467
-Right.
-It's a nice little sad one.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.501
Not too weepy...
-No.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.133
-... that you're like bawling.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.200
Because I have those books too,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.534
and I have to ban them
from my house

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.868
because I don't like them
for me or my child.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.200
-Don't want them reading them?
-No, I'm just like,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.934
"[ Crying ]
And then I love you."

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.534
[ Normal voice ] And then I go,
"I can't do that."

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:24.100
But this one, you go,
"Oh, this rhymes with that,"

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.434
and then I got to be super
creative,

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.300
and then we had a great artist
and they make animals

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.534
and the drawings
and all the stuff.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.133
And then you send it back
and give notes,

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.634
and then you have to send it,
and they have to make it

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.300
and it takes two years.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.300
So it's like wow.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.467
You're like I remember spending

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.934
every single day,
and now it's finally out.

